From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] explorer, winex11: the desktop's rubber band shows while dragging, and the icon under the pointer is lit, with an infotip

David (2026-10-06): "Dragging out a selection box does not render, but
still selects the items after you let go", and "when you hover over an
icon it should give you the full name of the app/filename, and kind of
highlight it".

The band was drawn (0630), but only onto the desktop window itself. With
the desktop's compositor running (sg-deskcomp, as on every installed
system), that window is under the compositor's canvas: what shows is the
desktop's picture, _SG_DESKTOP_PIXMAP (0744), and that picture was made
again only 300 ms after the desktop was last drawn -- while the mouse moved
the timer kept being pushed back, so the band never showed, and a click's
selection showed late. The parts of the desktop drawn again (the band as
it moves, an icon lit or selected, every paint) now also go into that
picture at once, in place, through a new display-driver escape
(X11DRV_SG_DESKTOP_PART: an XPutImage of the rectangle into the published
pixmap); sg-deskcomp (sg-compositor 0.2.0+sg43) paints them from the
pixmap's damage. The band redraws only what changed (where it grew or
shrank, its old and new borders, the icons it selected or let go), not
the union of both rectangles on every move.

Drawn as Windows draws them: the band in the accent colour, translucent,
with a solid one-pixel accent border (was a fixed lavender frame). Icons
have hot-tracking: the icon under the pointer gets a light box behind
icon and title (the accent's light tint, a stronger border), stronger
still when selected and under the pointer; after the hover delay an
infotip below the pointer gives the full name (a long one is cut short
under the icon) and, for a file, Type, Size and Date modified; for a
shortcut its comment or "Location:" of its target; for a folder its date;
for This PC, Recycle Bin and the other shell icons their CLSID's InfoTip.
Off the icon, onto a window or a click, both go. The boxes are round in
the Rounded (4 px) and Glass (3 px) looks, square in Classic and Horizon,
and scale with the display scale. The keyboard moves the focus as on
Windows' desktop: Home/End, the arrows (Shift extends from the anchor,
Ctrl moves the focus alone, Space and Ctrl+Space select and toggle); once
the keyboard is used the focused icon is marked with a one-pixel box,
until the next click. The desktop's dump (SG_DESKTOP_DUMP) gains hot=,
tip=, focus=, focuscues=, each icon's box and the infotip's text.

Test: test/deskhover-gate.sh (make test-deskhover) -- X alone, under
sg-deskcomp, and at 200 % with a light wallpaper and the Rounded look: the
band's pixels mid-drag while the mouse keeps moving, its accent border,
the selection on release, the lit box's pixels, the infotip's text and
place, the keyboard focus; mutants SG_MUTANT_BAND_UNPUBLISHED,
SG_MUTANT_NO_HOT, SG_MUTANT_NO_INFOTIP (explorer desktop.c) and
sg-deskcomp's SG_MUTANT_NO_BG_DAMAGE each fail it.
